          <h2>Cleanup and deduplication checklist</h2>
          <div class="guide-checklist"><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Duplicate definition agreed in writing</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Snapshot exported with original IDs</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Duplicate sources identified</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Primary-record rules documented</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Consent and ownership protected</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Test batch merged and checked</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Merge log kept</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Company domains normalised</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Integrations upsert on external IDs</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Weekly exception report live</div></div></div>
        </section>
        <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Do not measure cleanup by records merged. Measure the result: fewer routing errors, cleaner attribution, faster search, and reports people trust.</p></div>
